String is a class in Java and it can also act as a data type i.e. non-primitive datatype.
String is generally used to store a set of characters. 
This can be done in two ways.
a) literal b) new keyword.

a) Using String literal: It involves use of String keyword.
String name = "Abhishek";

b) Using new keyword: It involves object creation of the String class.
String name = new String("Abhishek");
